USER DEFINED ICONS
==================

You can use your own icons with the "User defined" icon style.

Create an icon file for every QWeather icon code you want to display,
named CODE.png (or CODE.svg, CODE.jpg, CODE.gif), for example:

  100.png   - sunny
  101.png   - cloudy
  104.png   - overcast
  305.png   - light rain
  400.png   - light snow
  999.png   - unknown (used as the fallback)

The complete list of icon codes is documented at
https://icons.qweather.com/en/

You may also add an iconmeta.json file to describe the set:

{
    "ext": "png",
    "aspect": 1,
    "adjust": 1,
    "map": {
        "104": "myOvercastIcon"
    }
}

* ext - the file extension of the icons (default png)
* aspect - width divided by height of the icons (default 1)
* adjust - scale factor applied to the icon (default 1)
* map - maps icon codes to file names

Icons missing from this directory fall back to the built-in QWeather icon set.
